            "text": "{\n  \"judgments\": [\n    {\n      \"proposal_id\": \"P0001\",\n      \"quotes\": [\n        \"If the eyeglasses are accepted for medical reasons:\",\n        \"(a) The frames of the eyeglasses must not cover the eye(s);\",\n        \"(b) There must not be glare on eyeglasses that obscures the eye(s);\",\n        \"(c) There must not be shadows or refraction from the eyeglasses that obscure the eye(s); and\",\n        \"(d) Dark or tinted lenses are permitted if the medical statement also indicates that they are required.\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"The source explicitly sets forth 'If the eyeglasses are accepted for medical reasons:' as the governing conditional heading directly introducing items (a) through (d), which correspond to claims C0017, C0018, C0019, and C0020. Adding this explicit condition qualification accurately models the textual scope across all four targeted rules without altering modal force or adding duplicate duties.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"supported\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
